  },
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "num": "01",
      "en": "Can a small group of drones ( (无人机) ) {guarantee} the {safety} and {reliability} of {railways} and, at the same time, help railway {operators} save {billions} of {euros} each year? That is the very likely future of applying today's “eyes in the sky” technology to make sure that more than one million kilometers of {rail} tracks and infrastructure ( (基础设施) ) {worldwide} are safe for trains 24/7.",
      "cn": "一小群无人机能否在 保障铁路安全可靠 的同时，还能帮助铁路 运营商 每年节省数 十亿欧元 呢？利用当今的“天眼”技术，确保 全球 100多万公里的 铁路 轨道和基础设施全天候安全运行，这很可能会成为未来的现实。"
    },
    {
      "num": "02",
      "en": "Drones are already being used to examine {high-tension electrical} lines.They could do precisely the same thing to {inspect} railway lines and other vital aspects of rail infrastructure, such as the correct position of railway tracks and the functioning of switching points.The more {regularly} they can be inspected, the more railway safety, reliability and on-time performance will be improved.Costs would be cut and {operations} would be more efficient across the board.",
      "cn": "无人机已经被用于检查 高压电 线。在 检查 铁路线路和基础设施的其他关键部分（如铁轨的位置是否正确、道岔的状态是否良好）时，无人机也能发挥同样的作用。 定期 检查越频繁，铁路的安全性、可靠性和准点率就会越高。成本会降低， 运营 效率也会全面提高。"
    },
    {
      "num": "03",
      "en": "That includes huge {savings} in {maintenance} costs and better {protection} of railway {personnel's} safety.It is {calculated} that European railways alone spend over 50 billion euros a year on maintenance, including sending maintenance staff to inspect and {repair} the rail infrastructure.That can be dangerous work, especially in {deserts} and {snowy} mountainous regions, which could be avoided with drones {assisting} the {crews’} efforts.",
      "cn": "这其中包括 节省 大量 维护 成本，以及更好地 保护 铁路工作 人员 的安全。据 计算 ，仅欧洲的铁路每年用于维护的花费就高达500多亿欧元，其中包括派遣维护人员检查和 修理 铁路基础设施。这可能是一项危险的工作，尤其是在 沙漠 和 雪 山地区，而有了无人机 协助工作人员 ，就可以避免这些危险。"
    },
    {
      "num": "04",
      "en": "Railway {officials} are recognizing the importance of drones in {defense} against potential accidents.By using the latest technologies, drones could detect {faults} in the rail or switches, before they cause any safety problems.For example, drones could provide real-time ( (实时的) ) {alerts} to approaching trains, when {kangaroos} or other wildlife wander onto the tracks in Australia.In regions with active {volcanoes} , drones can monitor their activities near railway lines, ensuring that {villages} and rail services are safe in case they {erupt} .",
      "cn": "铁路部门的 官员 正在认识到无人机在 防范 潜在事故方面的重要性。借助最新技术，无人机可以检测铁轨或 道岔 的 故障 ，以免其导致安全问题。例如，在澳大利亚，当 袋鼠 或其他野生动物闯入铁轨时，无人机可以向驶来的列车发出实时 警报 。在有活火山的地区，无人机可以监控铁路沿线附近的 火山 活动，在火山 爆发 时确保周边 村庄 和铁路服务的安全。"
    },
    {
      "num": "05",
      "en": "{Engineers} are now working on a new concept: the rail drones of the future.They will be moving on the track ahead of the train, and programmed to operate {autonomously} .Tiny drones with {advanced} sensors and AI travelling ahead of the train could guide it like a {co-pilot} .With their ability to see ahead, they could signal any problem, so that fast-moving trains would be able to {react} in time.In case of emergencies, drones could also assist in working with {ambulance} services.Additionally, the huge {volume} of data collected by drones can be analyzed to predict repair needs, benefiting both the repair {division} and {insurance} providers.As for the legal aspects, {consultation} with {lawyers} would be required to address the challenges of drone use.",
      "cn": "目前， 工程师 们正在研究一种新概念——未来铁路无人机。它们将在列车前方的轨道上空移动，并被 设定 为 自动 运行。微型无人机配备了 先进的 传感器和人工智能，当它们在列车前方飞行时，可以像 副驾驶员 一样引导列车行进。凭借观察前方的能力，无人机可以进行异常预警，从而让高速行驶的列车及时 作出反应 。在紧急情况下，无人机还能协助 救护车 服务。此外，无人机收集到的大 量 数据可以进行分析，以预测维修需求，这对维修 部门 和 保险 公司都有好处。至于法律方面的问题，则需要 咨询律师 ，以应对无人机使用带来的挑战。 5NoOncib/NjiX02BpMIzP4m+378Hw1xTRxUdPaP/PFjKUFq4K2G7tp6ZLYoCE601yW1W39VMdLmovFdSHs4nVQ=="
    }
  ],
